1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,104
[This drama is a work of fiction]

2
00:00:07,104 --> 00:00:08,192
[All scenes involving animals and children
were filmed in compliance with regulations]

3
00:00:12,049 --> 00:00:18,649
[The Day of the Incident]

4
00:00:22,096 --> 00:00:23,883
It burns well.

5
00:00:29,344 --> 00:00:33,224
But what about the phone and wallet?

6
00:00:33,224 --> 00:00:35,244
It's better to burn them all, right?

7
00:00:35,244 --> 00:00:36,912
Are you crazy?

8
00:00:36,912 --> 00:00:39,612
The phone could explode.

9
00:00:39,612 --> 00:00:42,016
And never turn it on.

10
00:00:46,724 --> 00:00:48,980
Then what should we do with this?

11
00:00:48,980 --> 00:00:51,083
Should we dump it somewhere else?

12
00:00:51,852 --> 00:00:55,783
But if we dump it somewhere carelessly
and someone finds it...

13
00:00:56,480 --> 00:00:58,180
Right.

14
00:00:59,483 --> 00:01:01,983
If someone turns the phone on somewhere else,

15
00:01:03,116 --> 00:01:05,516
they'll know that's where the person is.

16
00:01:08,832 --> 00:01:10,532
Wait a second.

17
00:01:12,440 --> 00:01:14,149
Then this...

18
00:01:16,504 --> 00:01:18,583
This credit card too.

19
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,149
If someone finds it
somewhere completely unrelated...

20
00:01:26,056 --> 00:01:28,649
No one will ever find us, right?

21
00:01:32,052 --> 00:01:34,252
Honey.

22
00:01:34,252 --> 00:01:36,549
Honey, I think we're geniuses.

23
00:01:37,376 --> 00:01:39,549
<i>But where should we dump this?</i>

24
00:01:42,366 --> 00:01:44,383
<i>Somewhere anyone can go.</i>

25
00:01:55,249 --> 00:02:01,016
[Public Restroom]

26
00:02:31,936 --> 00:02:35,992
<i>Somewhere you can easily spot it
when you're using a public restroom.</i>

27
00:02:35,992 --> 00:02:37,749
<i>You know that, right?</i>

28
00:03:08,583 --> 00:03:10,348
<i>Yeah, I'm done. What about the phone?</i>

29
00:03:10,348 --> 00:03:11,672
I don't think this is a good place.

30
00:03:11,672 --> 00:03:14,472
There are too many CCTV cameras in the park.

31
00:03:14,472 --> 00:03:17,716
I think there's got to be
a safer way to get rid of it.

32
00:03:28,216 --> 00:03:32,483
[Salt]

33
00:04:01,016 --> 00:04:05,916
[Episode 6, Your Mom, My Dad]

34
00:04:05,916 --> 00:04:08,584
So where are you going at this hour?

35
00:04:08,584 --> 00:04:11,249
I swear, I won't contact her again, ever.

36
00:04:11,249 --> 00:04:12,996
Look, honey. Honey, honey.

37
00:04:12,996 --> 00:04:13,996
Look at this.

38
00:04:13,996 --> 00:04:15,249
"Min Seo's mother".

39
00:04:15,249 --> 00:04:17,724
I'll block her right now,
right in front of you. I swear.

40
00:04:17,724 --> 00:04:18,816
Honey!

41
00:04:18,816 --> 00:04:22,224
I blocked her, see? Honey, look at this!

42
00:04:22,224 --> 00:04:24,783
I really won't contact her again. I swear!

43
00:04:24,783 --> 00:04:28,416
[Two Days After the Incident]

44
00:04:29,024 --> 00:04:31,983
Jeez, why did I do that? Seriously...

45
00:04:42,292 --> 00:04:45,783
Dad, did you and Mom fight?

46
00:04:46,724 --> 00:04:49,640
Was it because of me?

47
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:51,652
Is that why she left?

48
00:04:51,652 --> 00:04:53,916
N-No, Ye Ji.

49
00:04:53,916 --> 00:04:55,683
That's not it, Ye Ji.

50
00:04:57,199 --> 00:05:01,176
Ye Ji, this wasn't because of you.

51
00:05:01,176 --> 00:05:02,876
Okay?

52
00:05:53,796 --> 00:05:55,884
<i>Did I ask you to do something so difficult?
I only asked you to trust me.</i>

53
00:05:55,884 --> 00:05:58,428
<i>Go tell your dad everything!
Tell him you did nothing wrong.</i>

54
00:05:58,428 --> 00:06:00,116
<i>Tell him I'm the one who hit him, not you!</i>

55
00:06:00,116 --> 00:06:03,149
<i>Just say it! I should be the only one
who goes to prison!</i>

56
00:06:03,149 --> 00:06:05,349
<i>Isn't that what you want?</i>

57
00:07:12,352 --> 00:07:14,248
Hey, Ye Ji.

58
00:07:14,248 --> 00:07:16,149
<i>Min Seo.</i>

59
00:07:17,430 --> 00:07:19,130
Ye Ji...

60
00:07:24,252 --> 00:07:25,952
Are you crying?

61
00:07:26,684 --> 00:07:31,083
<i>My mom... left home.</i>

62
00:07:32,512 --> 00:07:35,116
<i>What am I supposed to do, Min Seo?</i>

63
00:07:42,008 --> 00:07:48,883
[Sorry, but can you check
whether the video was deleted?]

64
00:08:19,504 --> 00:08:22,436
[Gangnam Station]

65
00:08:22,436 --> 00:08:23,916
Yes, the comments have been pouring in.

66
00:08:23,916 --> 00:08:25,472
So many of our crew members

67
00:08:25,472 --> 00:08:27,572
have shown interest in Apel Kitchen.

68
00:08:27,572 --> 00:08:31,120
That's right. We recreated
Captain Park's Apel Kitchen right here.

69
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:33,716
I'll introduce it in more detail today.

70
00:08:33,716 --> 00:08:35,856
First of all,
the color is incredibly elegant.

71
00:08:35,856 --> 00:08:39,216
It's touch-operated,
so it's incredibly convenient.

72
00:08:39,216 --> 00:08:42,128
And it can be custom-made
to fit different spaces, right?

73
00:08:42,128 --> 00:08:44,658
Yeah, we offer customization.

74
00:08:44,658 --> 00:08:47,049
So you can choose the height, width,

75
00:08:47,049 --> 00:08:50,224
and even the color to suit your space.

76
00:08:50,224 --> 00:08:52,532
I especially love this part.

77
00:08:52,532 --> 00:08:55,300
I really like this Zen-style design.

78
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:57,024
You know, that's the thing about Zen-style.

79
00:08:57,024 --> 00:09:00,340
It gives you elegance and sophistication,
almost as if you've brought

80
00:09:00,340 --> 00:09:03,201
a work of art into your own space.

81
00:09:03,201 --> 00:09:05,604
Yes, our showroom is
right in front of Gangnam Station,

82
00:09:05,604 --> 00:09:07,788
so it's very convenient
for in-person consultations.

83
00:09:07,788 --> 00:09:10,224
It must be easy for you to get here too.

84
00:09:10,224 --> 00:09:13,424
Cut! Oh, that's great. That's great. Perfect.

85
00:09:13,424 --> 00:09:14,683
Okay, next shot!

86
00:09:14,683 --> 00:09:16,292
Please get this one more time.

87
00:09:16,292 --> 00:09:18,583
- Here?
- Yes, and then back here...

88
00:09:18,583 --> 00:09:21,149
Oh, over here. Min Su, Min Su!

89
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:25,080
Ugh, so tired.

90
00:09:26,783 --> 00:09:30,116
[My Hong: Please.
My Daughter: Did you fight with Dad?]

91
00:09:34,984 --> 00:09:36,252
- Min Su!
- Yes?

92
00:09:36,252 --> 00:09:38,272
- We should get this, this, and this.
- Yeah.

93
00:09:38,272 --> 00:09:41,283
Wait, the homeroom teacher keeps calling.

94
00:10:20,768 --> 00:10:22,604
You're saying you want
to take Min Seo right now?

95
00:10:22,604 --> 00:10:24,496
- Hello.
<i>- On what authority?</i>

96
00:10:24,496 --> 00:10:26,524
<i>Huh? What are you up to this time?</i>

97
00:10:26,524 --> 00:10:31,112
There was abuse and a missing-child report.
Anyone can see you're unfit to be a parent.

98
00:10:31,112 --> 00:10:33,916
You filed those fake reports yourself!

99
00:10:34,816 --> 00:10:37,383
You think I'm just going to
sit back and take it?

100
00:10:38,352 --> 00:10:40,144
What, are you going to sue me?

101
00:10:40,144 --> 00:10:44,049
Perfect. Attorney Choi
has been dying to meet you.

102
00:10:45,548 --> 00:10:46,844
Attorney Choi?

103
00:10:46,844 --> 00:10:48,656
Hello. It's been a while.

104
00:10:48,656 --> 00:10:51,583
She's a child abuser.
Please arrest her quickly.

105
00:10:57,140 --> 00:10:58,840
I don't care.

106
00:11:00,024 --> 00:11:03,016
So please speak
with Attorney Choi from now on.

107
00:11:03,752 --> 00:11:04,968
Hello.

108
00:11:04,968 --> 00:11:06,983
Yes, thank you for your hard work.

109
00:11:06,983 --> 00:11:08,649
[Jewelry Dermatology, Grand Open,
Completion scheduled for late April!]

110
00:11:08,649 --> 00:11:09,916
Ms. Park, you're here.

111
00:11:09,916 --> 00:11:10,949
You're here, Ms. Park.

112
00:11:10,949 --> 00:11:13,283
- You're here?
- Oh, Dr. Joo.

113
00:11:25,004 --> 00:11:26,152
Ye Ji!

114
00:11:26,152 --> 00:11:30,172
I couldn't tell you yesterday,
but about that video, did you...

115
00:11:30,172 --> 00:11:31,872
Yeah, Dad.

116
00:11:32,856 --> 00:11:34,556
Huh?

117
00:11:40,348 --> 00:11:41,349
Taxi!

118
00:11:41,349 --> 00:11:45,216
[Vacant]

119
00:12:07,983 --> 00:12:10,649
<i>Please leave a message after the beep...</i>

120
00:12:15,449 --> 00:12:19,520
[Why aren't you answering? Is the job done?
Let me know when you confirm.]

121
00:12:26,420 --> 00:12:28,832
[Min Seo's Academy]

122
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:31,720
Yeah, yeah.

123
00:12:34,092 --> 00:12:35,949
Min Seo?

124
00:12:45,324 --> 00:12:46,848
Oh no...

125
00:12:46,848 --> 00:12:47,968
Y-You're awake.

126
00:12:47,968 --> 00:12:50,388
- I didn't mean to wake you...
- Oh my, I'm so sorry.

127
00:12:50,388 --> 00:12:52,016
- Careful.
- Thank you.

128
00:12:52,016 --> 00:12:53,452
There's still some left.

129
00:12:53,452 --> 00:12:55,616
You must've been startled.

130
00:12:55,616 --> 00:12:58,200
I'm not usually the type to faint.

131
00:12:58,200 --> 00:13:01,740
Is there a specific type
of person who faints?

132
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:04,472
Let me see. I think it's all in there.

133
00:13:04,472 --> 00:13:06,983
- Okay, I'll get it out for you.
- Okay.

134
00:13:12,308 --> 00:13:15,732
Oh dear, you really regret it
once you lose it

135
00:13:15,732 --> 00:13:18,449
if you don't take care of it beforehand.

136
00:13:19,756 --> 00:13:21,456
I know.

137
00:13:22,228 --> 00:13:25,049
What if I've already lost everything
and regret it?

138
00:13:27,496 --> 00:13:28,780
Right here... yeah.

139
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:30,983
- Oh, yes.
- Keep pressing down here.

140
00:13:32,844 --> 00:13:34,583
Actually, for me too,

141
00:13:35,244 --> 00:13:37,816
it's not that I'm expanding the hospital.

142
00:13:39,368 --> 00:13:42,083
My ex-wife took everything from me.

143
00:13:43,232 --> 00:13:47,449
I just gave her the kid and the house,
and afterward...

144
00:13:47,449 --> 00:13:49,928
I thought nothing was going right.

145
00:13:49,928 --> 00:13:52,752
But now that I've opened a new clinic

146
00:13:52,752 --> 00:13:54,512
and you handled

147
00:13:54,512 --> 00:13:58,124
all the interior work,
I feel like I can get back on my feet.

148
00:13:58,124 --> 00:14:00,016
- You're here.
- Oh, yes.

149
00:14:01,204 --> 00:14:06,308
Well, neither the kid nor the husband
ever does what I want.

150
00:14:06,308 --> 00:14:08,272
- Here, this way!
- Oh, is it not this way?

151
00:14:08,272 --> 00:14:09,968
Life isn't all that complicated, really.

152
00:14:09,968 --> 00:14:12,849
- You just keep going, that's all.
- Mom!

153
00:14:14,116 --> 00:14:15,492
- Honey!
- Oh, yes.

154
00:14:15,492 --> 00:14:17,680
Ye Ji.

155
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:21,260
Ms. Yoon called and said
you suddenly collapsed.

156
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:24,924
Honey, are you feeling okay?

157
00:14:24,924 --> 00:14:26,383
Dr. Joo, let me explain this for a moment...

158
00:14:26,383 --> 00:14:28,072
You must've had a rough time.

159
00:14:28,072 --> 00:14:30,216
Let's go home quickly.

160
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:34,508
For the lighting you asked for,
we'll put two magnetic fixtures here.

161
00:14:34,508 --> 00:14:36,556
And we'll probably do recessed lighting here.

162
00:14:36,556 --> 00:14:38,256
- Oh, right here?
- Yes, that's right.

163
00:14:38,256 --> 00:14:39,908
Is there any other lighting you'd like...

164
00:14:39,908 --> 00:14:41,468
Let's go home.

165
00:14:41,468 --> 00:14:45,249
Yeah, okay. Let's go home.
Get some rest at home, honey.

166
00:15:36,192 --> 00:15:37,892
Min Seo!

167
00:15:39,024 --> 00:15:40,716
Mom!

168
00:15:40,716 --> 00:15:42,128
Why did you come here again?

169
00:15:42,128 --> 00:15:44,184
I'm really scared, Mom.

170
00:15:44,184 --> 00:15:46,124
What do I do?

171
00:15:46,124 --> 00:15:48,224
It's okay, Min Seo.

172
00:15:48,224 --> 00:15:49,712
It'll be okay.

173
00:15:49,712 --> 00:15:53,749
Mommy will make sure of it.

174
00:16:16,516 --> 00:16:19,616
[My Child Guardian: GTS child
location-sharing app installation]

175
00:16:19,616 --> 00:16:20,616
[Installing...]

176
00:16:20,616 --> 00:16:21,632
[Installed]

177
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:07,180
Well...

178
00:17:26,116 --> 00:17:31,783
[Five Days After the Incident]

179
00:17:51,924 --> 00:17:53,140
Huh?

180
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:57,478
Y-You're giving these to me as a gift?

181
00:17:57,478 --> 00:17:59,408
I got these as a gift a long time ago,

182
00:17:59,408 --> 00:18:02,482
but I never really had
an occasion to wear them.

183
00:18:02,482 --> 00:18:06,620
Well, in life, people can change their shoes,

184
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:09,636
but you're actually giving me these?

185
00:18:09,636 --> 00:18:13,372
Even if it wasn't intentional,
refusing to return them

186
00:18:13,372 --> 00:18:17,252
could still constitute
misappropriation of lost property.

187
00:18:17,252 --> 00:18:20,308
Oh, don't call it misappropriation.

188
00:18:20,308 --> 00:18:22,112
Goodness.

189
00:18:22,112 --> 00:18:25,232
Are you a lawyer?

190
00:18:25,232 --> 00:18:28,136
Oh, yes. Well, I just run a small practice.

191
00:18:28,136 --> 00:18:31,549
Oh, I see.

192
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:38,040
These are really hard to find.

193
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:40,116
Are they very expensive?

194
00:18:41,336 --> 00:18:43,384
Oh dear, you really have no idea.

195
00:18:43,384 --> 00:18:45,649
Wow, this is really something...

196
00:18:50,584 --> 00:18:53,808
Sol came by here not long ago, right?

197
00:18:53,808 --> 00:18:56,948
Yes, he came with another customer.

198
00:18:56,948 --> 00:18:58,696
Is that him?

199
00:18:58,696 --> 00:19:01,049
Yeah, that's him.

200
00:19:03,948 --> 00:19:06,349
Did he say anything unusual?

201
00:19:08,556 --> 00:19:10,256
Anything unusual?

202
00:19:11,144 --> 00:19:13,932
Oh, I heard he was some kind of lawyer.

203
00:19:13,932 --> 00:19:15,222
A lawyer?

204
00:19:15,222 --> 00:19:19,416
Yes, Mr. Na Sol told me
to take special care of him.

205
00:19:24,149 --> 00:19:27,249
I don't think he's a lawyer.

206
00:19:50,560 --> 00:19:52,048
Take a look.

207
00:19:52,048 --> 00:19:53,640
[Representative Attorney at CP Law Firm]
His name is Choi Sang Cheol.

208
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:54,764
He's a lawyer.

209
00:19:54,764 --> 00:19:55,764
[Recent Wins: 'Hanram-dong Drug Party'
chaebol's second son acquitted]

210
00:19:55,764 --> 00:19:59,049
Look, this guy handled
the Hanram-dong drug party case

211
00:19:59,049 --> 00:20:02,316
and that huge prostitution case
recently, you know.

212
00:20:02,316 --> 00:20:04,764
He defended that case too.

213
00:20:04,764 --> 00:20:07,516
Basically, if there's money to be made,
he'll blackmail, forge documents,

214
00:20:07,516 --> 00:20:09,456
do whatever it takes.

215
00:20:09,456 --> 00:20:13,116
I probably shouldn't say this,
but he's a complete gangster.

216
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:17,744
He doesn't seem big enough
to take on Na Sol himself.

217
00:20:17,744 --> 00:20:20,949
What, does he have some connections?

218
00:20:20,949 --> 00:20:23,016
Look.

219
00:20:23,016 --> 00:20:24,749
I'm a bit cautious about this, but...

220
00:20:24,749 --> 00:20:25,960
['Maguk-dong Murder Suspect'
Go Du Sik Released, Rule of Law in Question]

221
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:27,524
What's this?

222
00:20:27,524 --> 00:20:29,408
Remember the Maguk-dong dismemberment case

223
00:20:29,408 --> 00:20:32,388
and its suspect, Go Du Sik?

224
00:20:32,388 --> 00:20:36,992
The case was closed with no charges
due to insufficient evidence.

225
00:20:36,992 --> 00:20:42,316
But look here.
This was Choi Sang Cheol's doing.

226
00:20:42,316 --> 00:20:44,796
That's what makes it suspicious.

227
00:20:44,796 --> 00:20:46,983
It was obviously an airtight case.

228
00:20:46,983 --> 00:20:50,544
And yet it ended with an acquittal,

229
00:20:50,544 --> 00:20:53,432
which means Go Du Sik must be

230
00:20:53,432 --> 00:20:56,048
fiercely loyal to Choi Sang Cheol.

231
00:20:56,048 --> 00:20:58,796
So if there's someone
pulling the strings behind this,

232
00:20:58,796 --> 00:21:02,760
Go Du Sik is our likely candidate, yeah.

233
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:04,060
Well...

234
00:21:04,060 --> 00:21:08,083
Can you track Choi Sang Cheol
and Go Du Sik's locations?

235
00:21:09,324 --> 00:21:11,872
Go Du Sik is doable,

236
00:21:11,872 --> 00:21:15,349
but Choi Sang Cheol...

237
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:21,796
You know, these days,

238
00:21:21,796 --> 00:21:24,668
security's really tight, yeah.

239
00:21:24,668 --> 00:21:27,760
And if we mess with a lawyer like that
and things go south,

240
00:21:27,760 --> 00:21:32,148
we'd be in trouble as well.

241
00:21:32,148 --> 00:21:34,292
Well then,

242
00:21:34,292 --> 00:21:36,732
let's meet Go Du Sik and talk to him first.

243
00:21:36,732 --> 00:21:38,612
Yeah. Peacefully.

244
00:21:38,612 --> 00:21:41,116
What? You mean meet Go Du Sik in person?

245
00:21:44,116 --> 00:21:47,192
What were you doing on March 30?

246
00:21:47,192 --> 00:21:51,016
March 30? Well... what did I do?

247
00:21:55,968 --> 00:21:58,183
Ah, darn it, I can't remember.

248
00:22:01,168 --> 00:22:02,456
Have a drink of this.

249
00:22:02,456 --> 00:22:04,649
It'll clear your head.

250
00:22:08,656 --> 00:22:10,536
My head's clear already.

251
00:22:10,536 --> 00:22:13,116
You don't look very clear-headed.

252
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:19,140
Well...

253
00:22:20,683 --> 00:22:23,349
Can I take a quick look at your phone?

254
00:22:31,992 --> 00:22:33,724
Why do you need my phone?

255
00:22:33,724 --> 00:22:36,749
It'll only take a second.

256
00:22:38,124 --> 00:22:40,056
