or a work meeting?

339
00:28:15,932 --> 00:28:16,949
- Hello.
- No.

340
00:28:16,949 --> 00:28:18,768
Oh, Min Seo. Hello.

341
00:28:18,768 --> 00:28:20,883
What do you mean, no?

342
00:28:20,883 --> 00:28:25,083
It's not a work meeting?
Or it's not a lunch appointment?

343
00:28:26,064 --> 00:28:28,612
Honey, want to have dinner together later?

344
00:28:28,612 --> 00:28:31,252
Honey, where will you be done later?
I'll come to you, okay?

345
00:28:31,252 --> 00:28:32,952
It's okay.

346
00:28:35,792 --> 00:28:38,864
Honey! Drive safely, okay?

347
00:28:38,864 --> 00:28:40,564
See you.

348
00:28:51,364 --> 00:28:54,549
Jae Hong! Why aren't you
answering your phone?

349
00:28:55,692 --> 00:28:57,696
We can't do this, Ms. Ahn.

350
00:28:57,696 --> 00:28:59,583
Oh, that's not it...

351
00:29:00,996 --> 00:29:03,196
When you act like this, Soo Jung,
it's really hard for me.

352
00:29:03,196 --> 00:29:05,900
Let's just leave the good memories
as good memories, okay?

353
00:29:05,900 --> 00:29:08,336
Soo Jung, I'm begging you!

354
00:29:08,336 --> 00:29:10,649
That's not it. It's about Choi Sang Cheol!

355
00:29:20,736 --> 00:29:22,436
Why so quiet?

356
00:29:24,649 --> 00:29:26,324
What is going on?

357
00:29:26,324 --> 00:29:28,349
You two didn't have a fight, did you?

358
00:29:28,980 --> 00:29:31,036
Of course not.

359
00:29:31,036 --> 00:29:33,344
We're solid.

360
00:29:33,344 --> 00:29:35,083
Right, Min Seo?

361
00:29:36,092 --> 00:29:37,500
Huh?

362
00:29:37,500 --> 00:29:39,383
Yeah, yeah...

363
00:29:44,816 --> 00:29:47,212
- Ma'am.
- Yeah.

364
00:29:47,212 --> 00:29:49,349
By the way...

365
00:29:51,032 --> 00:29:54,283
did you delete the video?

366
00:29:56,836 --> 00:29:58,832
Oh...

367
00:29:58,832 --> 00:30:00,545
I'll...

368
00:30:01,998 --> 00:30:04,283
I'll take care of that myself.

369
00:30:04,932 --> 00:30:07,860
Well, of course,
I'm sure you handled it properly,

370
00:30:07,860 --> 00:30:09,448
but I heard that

371
00:30:09,448 --> 00:30:13,428
if you only delete the video,
it's safer to format the USB.

372
00:30:13,428 --> 00:30:14,744
If it's a hassle, I can do it for you...

373
00:30:14,744 --> 00:30:16,756
Min Seo.

374
00:30:16,756 --> 00:30:18,516
Don't worry about it.

375
00:30:24,483 --> 00:30:27,583
Yeah, don't worry too much, Min Seo.

376
00:30:33,836 --> 00:30:35,544
- Really?
- Yeah.

377
00:30:35,544 --> 00:30:39,504
Wait, Choi Sang Cheol is
your ex-husband's lawyer?

378
00:30:39,504 --> 00:30:40,596
Yeah.

379
00:30:40,596 --> 00:30:43,292
How could that just happen by chance?

380
00:30:43,292 --> 00:30:47,344
What if he approached you intentionally,
rather than it being a coincidence?

381
00:30:47,344 --> 00:30:49,116
Huh?

382
00:30:49,116 --> 00:30:51,380
What are you talking about all of a sudden?

383
00:30:51,380 --> 00:30:55,700
I think Choi Sang Cheol approached you

384
00:30:55,700 --> 00:30:58,892
to use our relationship in the lawsuit.
So think carefully.

385
00:30:58,892 --> 00:31:01,049
Did Choi Sang Cheol really say anything else?

386
00:31:01,049 --> 00:31:04,883
Jae Hong, you didn't tell him anything
you shouldn't have, did you?

387
00:31:06,416 --> 00:31:11,483
Well, I was so drunk that night,
I can barely remember.

388
00:31:11,483 --> 00:31:15,200
That punk. No wonder
he suddenly gave me those shoes.

389
00:31:15,200 --> 00:31:16,924
They're not even easy to find.

390
00:31:16,924 --> 00:31:18,988
The shoes?

391
00:31:18,988 --> 00:31:21,972
I don't think I told him anything important.

392
00:31:21,972 --> 00:31:26,888
But I was so drunk

393
00:31:26,888 --> 00:31:28,712
my memory is kind of...

394
00:31:28,712 --> 00:31:30,576
You don't remember?

395
00:31:30,576 --> 00:31:31,668
No.

396
00:31:31,668 --> 00:31:33,664
Jae Hong, here you are.

397
00:31:33,664 --> 00:31:35,420
Yeah, why are you here so early?

398
00:31:35,420 --> 00:31:36,524
We're late.

399
00:31:36,524 --> 00:31:38,852
Oh, really? Let's go.

400
00:31:38,852 --> 00:31:41,249
- Let's talk on Gogo Used Market later.
- Wait...

401
00:31:42,324 --> 00:31:43,920
Darn it.

402
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:47,416
Right, there's no way that punk
would just give those away. Darn it.

403
00:31:53,304 --> 00:31:54,752
Did he drug my drink that night?

404
00:31:54,752 --> 00:31:56,104
What? Drug?

405
00:31:56,104 --> 00:31:58,348
Huh?

406
00:31:58,348 --> 00:32:00,416
No, no, nothing.

407
00:32:00,416 --> 00:32:01,416
[Attorney Choi Sang Cheol, My Little Bro]

408
00:32:01,416 --> 00:32:03,316
This punk, seriously.

409
00:32:05,052 --> 00:32:06,892
<i>Hello? Oh, bro.</i>

410
00:32:06,892 --> 00:32:08,052
<i>Are you feeling okay?</i>

411
00:32:08,052 --> 00:32:09,583
<i>We should have another drink.</i>

412
00:32:09,583 --> 00:32:12,216
<i>Oh, how about we have it
at your place this time?</i>

413
00:32:12,216 --> 00:32:14,320
<i>I've got an amazing bottle of whiskey ready.</i>

414
00:32:14,320 --> 00:32:15,440
<i>I'll bring it over to your place.</i>

415
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:17,576
You...

416
00:32:17,576 --> 00:32:20,224
You really used to work out at that gym?

417
00:32:20,224 --> 00:32:21,456
<i>What?</i>

418
00:32:21,456 --> 00:32:23,300
How come I don't remember
ever seeing you there?

419
00:32:23,300 --> 00:32:25,083
<i>I usually go in the morning,
so maybe you just missed it.</i>

420
00:32:25,083 --> 00:32:28,744
And those shoes.

421
00:32:28,744 --> 00:32:31,792
You got those shoes as a gift,
never wore them, shoved them away,

422
00:32:31,792 --> 00:32:33,812
and then gave them to me.
Are you sure that's what happened?

423
00:32:33,812 --> 00:32:35,936
<i>Bro, what do you mean? Hold on...</i>

424
00:32:35,936 --> 00:32:38,083
<i>Oh, bro, hold on. Just a moment.
I have something to tell you first.</i>

425
00:32:38,083 --> 00:32:40,184
Forget it.

426
00:32:40,184 --> 00:32:41,372
Hang up, you punk.

427
00:32:41,372 --> 00:32:43,849
<i>Wait, wait, wait. Bro, hold on...</i>

428
00:32:48,483 --> 00:32:49,583
[Attorney Choi Sang Cheol, My Little Bro]

429
00:32:49,583 --> 00:32:51,683
That punk, darn it.

430
00:32:54,556 --> 00:32:56,256
Huh?

431
00:32:57,016 --> 00:32:58,456
[I think there's a misunderstanding.
Let's meet up.]

432
00:32:58,456 --> 00:33:00,012
[I'll come to your place
with the whiskey I mentioned.]

433
00:33:00,012 --> 00:33:02,049
Misunderstanding, my foot.

434
00:33:05,249 --> 00:33:06,784
[No, don't come]

435
00:33:23,772 --> 00:33:25,068
Ms. Kyung Hee.

436
00:33:25,068 --> 00:33:27,132
- Yes, Dr. Joo. Hello.
- Oh, my.

437
00:33:27,132 --> 00:33:30,904
Wow, you look absolutely beautiful as always.

438
00:33:30,904 --> 00:33:32,276
Oh my, stop it.

439
00:33:32,276 --> 00:33:36,340
Wait, I think everyone's
going to be staring at you.

440
00:33:36,340 --> 00:33:39,588
But are you really okay
with people recognizing you?

441
00:33:39,588 --> 00:33:41,640
Well, what's the big deal?

442
00:33:41,640 --> 00:33:43,580
We're here to talk business.

443
00:33:43,580 --> 00:33:44,600
Exactly. Business.

444
00:33:44,600 --> 00:33:46,992
Then shall we head up to the lounge
and talk properly?

445
00:33:46,992 --> 00:33:49,049
- Sure.
- All right, let's go.

446
00:33:55,336 --> 00:33:57,036
What's wrong?

447
00:34:04,352 --> 00:34:05,972
Huh? That person...

448
00:34:05,972 --> 00:34:08,149
She's Chairwoman Michelle's secretary.

449
00:34:08,860 --> 00:34:11,483
Oh, I guess the chairwoman is here.

450
00:34:11,483 --> 00:34:13,616
She's a regular here.

451
00:34:22,696 --> 00:34:23,749
Is something wrong?

452
00:34:23,749 --> 00:34:26,916
[Director Kwak: Driving]

453
00:34:34,516 --> 00:34:37,916
[Why aren't you answering? Is the job done?
Let me know when you confirm.]

454
00:34:50,488 --> 00:34:52,188
No way...

455
00:35:24,140 --> 00:35:31,098
[The person hit by the car,
do you remember what he looked like?]

456
00:35:35,749 --> 00:35:39,883
[I don't want to talk about that anymore.
It's too scary]

457
00:35:47,520 --> 00:35:54,482
[T.D.A]

458
00:36:29,648 --> 00:36:31,348
What are you doing?

459
00:36:33,944 --> 00:36:35,396
Mr. Na Sol!

460
00:36:35,396 --> 00:36:36,988
What is this, seriously?

461
00:36:36,988 --> 00:36:39,383
I thought you were dead.

462
00:36:41,372 --> 00:36:43,072
Dead?

463
00:36:45,140 --> 00:36:46,840
I mean...

464
00:36:47,532 --> 00:36:51,560
You said everything was taken care of,
so I even transferred the final payment.

465
00:36:51,560 --> 00:36:54,044
But that lawyer guy, huh?

466
00:36:54,044 --> 00:36:56,932
Instead of dropping the lawsuit,
he's even approached my neighbor

467
00:36:56,932 --> 00:36:59,304
- trying to dig up information about me...
- A lawyer?

468
00:36:59,304 --> 00:37:01,408
You mean Choi Sang Cheol?

469
00:37:01,408 --> 00:37:06,004
Yeah! I don't know
what Choi Sang Cheol is up to,

470
00:37:06,004 --> 00:37:09,304
but he's been drinking
with my neighbor and...

471
00:37:09,304 --> 00:37:10,716
How on earth did you handle this

472
00:37:10,716 --> 00:37:14,520
to make Choi Sang Cheol act up even more?

473
00:37:14,520 --> 00:37:16,220
Huh?

474
00:37:27,336 --> 00:37:30,628
Are you seriously going to pretend
you don't know anything

475
00:37:30,628 --> 00:37:32,852
after taking all the money?

476
00:37:32,852 --> 00:37:36,984
How can you be so rude?

477
00:37:36,984 --> 00:37:40,116
When were you told it would be taken care of?

478
00:37:41,228 --> 00:37:43,249
Why do you ask?

479
00:37:46,120 --> 00:37:47,820
Jeez.

480
00:37:49,368 --> 00:37:51,068
It was this day.

481
00:37:52,220 --> 00:37:54,016
March 30?

482
00:37:54,016 --> 00:37:57,544
Yeah. You sent me this message on the 30th,

483
00:37:57,544 --> 00:38:00,452
and I transferred the balance
the very next day.

484
00:38:00,452 --> 00:38:02,816
And you haven't been in touch since?

485
00:38:04,232 --> 00:38:07,483
You're the one who hasn't been answering,
Mr. Na Sol.

486
00:38:08,956 --> 00:38:13,108
That neighbor who's with Choi Sang Cheol.

487
00:38:13,108 --> 00:38:15,983
Shall we talk about him?

488
00:38:17,160 --> 00:38:18,984
What do you mean I've changed?

489
00:38:18,984 --> 00:38:20,983
You won't even listen
when I talk about the video,

490
00:38:20,983 --> 00:38:23,796
and you stop me every time
I try to talk to your mom.

491
00:38:23,796 --> 00:38:25,464
Even earlier, you just took your mom's side.

492
00:38:25,464 --> 00:38:27,524
When did I take her side?

493
00:38:27,524 --> 00:38:29,516
That's really not it.

494
00:38:30,192 --> 00:38:33,316
I told you my mom and dad
have been fighting like crazy because of me.

495
00:38:33,316 --> 00:38:36,249
What if they actually get divorced
because of this?

496
00:38:46,364 --> 00:38:48,480
I'm sorry.

497
00:38:48,480 --> 00:38:50,283
It's my fault.

498
00:38:52,096 --> 00:38:54,300
Are you really that afraid of divorce?

499
00:38:54,300 --> 00:38:57,560
So afraid that you can't even
ask them to delete the video?

500
00:38:57,560 --> 00:39:00,836
No, that's really not what I meant...

501
00:39:00,836 --> 00:39:03,796
If you didn't mean it,
then why aren't you doing anything?

502
00:39:03,796 --> 00:39:07,683
I'm freaking out, but how can you be so calm?

503
00:39:08,852 --> 00:39:10,676
That's not it...

504
00:39:10,676 --> 00:39:13,880
It's just that my mom and dad
have been fighting every single day lately...

505
00:39:13,880 --> 00:39:16,083
Is it because you weren't the one driving?

506
00:39:17,836 --> 00:39:19,536
What...

507
00:39:20,872 --> 00:39:22,572
You...

508
00:39:23,312 --> 00:39:25,883
I even lied to my parents to protect you!

509
00:39:25,883 --> 00:39:30,149
So you think you've done nothing wrong
and that this is all my fault, don't you?

510
00:39:30,776 --> 00:39:35,596
Otherwise, you would've gone
and deleted the video yourself by now.

511
00:39:35,596 --> 00:39:37,296
Is that right?

512
00:39:40,896 --> 00:39:42,636
Yeah, she said she'd head
straight home after the meeting?

513
00:39:42,636 --> 00:39:43,956
I understand now, yes.

514
00:39:43,956 --> 00:39:46,316
Okay, I'll call you back.

515
00:39:47,800 --> 00:39:49,500
Why...

516
00:39:50,804 --> 00:39:52,588
What's wrong?

517
00:39:52,588 --> 00:39:57,883
I only heard this secondhand,
so I'm a little hesitant to say,

518
00:39:57,883 --> 00:40:00,548
but apparently there's talk

519
00:40:00,548 --> 00:40:04,616
of changing the investment terms
to have Director Kwak as the CEO.

520
00:40:06,216 --> 00:40:10,949
And there's also talk of embezzlement.

521
00:40:10,949 --> 00:40:14,276
I don't know how much of it is true,

522
00:40:14,276 --> 00:40:17,683
but I think you should
look into it right away.

523
00:40:19,820 --> 00:40:21,883
Okay, just a moment...

524
00:40:24,488 --> 00:40:26,188
Yes.

525
00:40:26,916 --> 00:40:30,844
On the 13th,
publish the investment announcement first,

526
00:40:30,844 --> 00:40:32,612
and then...

527
00:40:32,612 --> 00:40:35,044
Wait, hold on.

528
00:40:35,044 --> 00:40:36,744
What...

529
00:40:38,216 --> 00:40:39,916
What?

530
00:40:40,700 --> 00:40:42,191
Shall I take you home after this?

531
00:40:42,191 --> 00:40:43,891
Yeah.

532
00:40:46,652 --> 00:40:48,880
Hello, Chairwoman.

533
00:40:48,880 --> 00:40:50,524
How did you know I'm here?

534
00:40:50,524 --> 00:40:53,383
I don't like dragging things out.

535
00:40:54,436 --> 00:40:56,283
So I'll get straight to the point.

536
00:40:59,820 --> 00:41:01,520
Is it true

537
00:41:02,436 --> 00:41:05,683
that replacing me with Director Kwak
is a condition

538
00:41:06,396 --> 00:41:08,096
of the investment?

539
00:41:19,040 --> 00:41:21,364
You were so concerned about our reputation

540
00:41:21,364 --> 00:41:24,383
that you even took issue
with our private life as a couple.

541
00:41:25,668 --> 00:41:26,683
I'm disappointed.

542
00:41:26,683 --> 00:41:29,416
Ms. Park, let's talk about this later...

543
00:41:32,468 --> 00:41:37,596
The brand value of the ZiP is me,
Park Kyung Hee.

544
00:41:37,596 --> 00:41:39,792
If you go through with this backroom deal,

545
00:41:39,792 --> 00:41:42,149
my name, my face, and my family
will all be pulled

546
00:41:42,149 --> 00:41:43,972
from the ZiP immediately.

547
00:41:43,972 --> 00:41:46,216
And I'll make sure everyone hears about it.

548
00:41:48,683 --> 00:41:51,012
If you're willing to tarnish
the reputation you've built

549
00:41:51,012 --> 00:41:54,117
just to invest in a company that's been
stripped down to nothing,

550
00:41:54,117 --> 00:41:55,883
then go ahead.

551
00:42:02,952 --> 00:42:07,516
Ms. Park, I've always
liked this bold side of you.

552
00:42:10,952 --> 00:42:12,652
Have a look.

553
00:42:23,300 --> 00:42:25,000
Oh...

554
00:42:25,808 --> 00:42:27,633
This 300 million won

555
00:42:27,633 --> 00:42:30,249
was an unavoidable loss
from paying for materials

556
00:42:30,249 --> 00:42:34,212
- for the company...
- Isn't it better to remain the face of the ZiP

557
00:42:34,212 --> 00:42:39,216
than to go down as some petty criminal
who embezzled from her own company?

558
00:42:45,980 --> 00:42:47,516
Kyung Hee,

559
00:42:47,516 --> 00:42:52,716
think carefully about what's really best
for saving the company, okay?

560
00:43:02,776 --> 00:43:04,476
Hey!

561
00:43:06,020 --> 00:43:07,720
What?

562
00:43:09,664 --> 00:43:12,272
Did you tell Michelle

563
00:43:12,272 --> 00:43:15,116
I embezzled money,
so you could take over the company?

564
00:44:03,624 --> 00:44:04,980
Are you all right?

565
00:44:04,980 --> 00:44:07,383
Yeah, I'm fine.

566
00:44:08,376 --> 00:44:12,983
Oh dear, I was just really worried about you.

567
00:44:14,388 --> 00:44:15,956
I'm fine.

568
00:44:15,956 --> 00:44:20,052
But are you really okay to drive?

569
00:44:20,052 --> 00:44:22,620
Oh, it's fine.

570
00:44:22,620 --> 00:44:24,416
I'm really fine.

571
00:44:26,544 --> 00:44:30,080
Well, when I'm in business,
this kind of thing happens all the time.

572
00:44:30,080 --> 00:44:32,808
But what a shame about today.

573
00:44:32,808 --> 00:44:33,996
We didn't even get to
talk business today, Dr. Joo.

574
00:44:33,996 --> 00:44:35,852
- I'm sorry.
- What...

575
00:44:35,852 --> 00:44:38,016
What are you apologizing for?

576
00:44:42,076 --> 00:44:43,776
Ms. Kyung Hee,

577
00:44:45,156 --> 00:44:46,983
when things get hard,

578
00:44:48,428 --> 00:44:52,283
you don't have to pretend you're fine.

579
00:44:52,992 --> 00:44:54,692
Okay?

580
00:45:00,536 --> 00:45:02,283
It's okay.

581
00:45:03,916 --> 00:45:05,616
It's okay.

582
00:45:09,824 --> 00:45:11,524
It's okay...

583
00:45:14,736 --> 00:45:16,436
It's okay.

584
00:45:18,500 --> 00:45:20,200
It's fine.

585
00:45:20,816 --> 00:45:21,940
It's fine.

586
00:45:21,940 --> 00:45:24,712
Oh, wait...

587
00:45:24,712 --> 00:45:25,712
What?

588
00:45:25,712 --> 00:45:27,616
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Oh...

589
00:45:30,140 --> 00:45:32,883
My apologies, I was out of line.

590
00:45:37,648 --> 00:45:40,216
Then I'll be going.

591
00:45:40,964 --> 00:45:43,283
Take extra care when you drive, really.

592
00:45:44,796 --> 00:45:46,496
Yeah.

593
00:45:53,708 --> 00:45:55,583
Get home safely.

594
00:46:13,883 --> 00:46:17,248
[But how on earth did Sang Cheol
find out about our relationship?]

595
00:46:19,283 --> 00:46:21,120
[I don't know]

596
00:46:24,716 --> 00:46:25,716
[Did he have us followed or something?]

597
00:46:25,716 --> 00:46:29,088
[He knows everything, so why approach me?
What more is there to gain?]

598
00:46:32,816 --> 00:46:35,872
[Could it be our video... no way...]

599
00:46:37,888 --> 00:46:39,588
The video?

600
00:46:49,216 --> 00:46:51,983
[Could we use that private investigator
I told you about and dig into Sang Cheol?]

601
00:46:51,983 --> 00:46:53,792
[If this gets out, I'm in serious trouble]

602
00:46:55,464 --> 00:46:57,249
Oh, seriously...

603
00:46:59,149 --> 00:47:01,952
[Because of that private investigator
you introduced me to, I'm now...]

604
00:47:04,883 --> 00:47:06,249
[The guy from the agency you recommended
has been acting strange]

605
00:47:06,249 --> 00:47:07,516
[and barely answering my calls
since he met Choi Sang Cheol]

606
00:47:07,516 --> 00:47:08,864
[I went there myself, but he wouldn't
answer me and avoided even mentioning it]

607
00:47:10,516 --> 00:47:12,416
[What if they're in cahoots?]

608
00:47:15,160 --> 00:47:18,083
Choi Sang Cheol... and Na Sol?

609
00:47:21,816 --> 00:47:24,896
[This guy, Na Sol,
hasn't come looking for you, has he?]

610
00:47:25,512 --> 00:47:27,320
You spin and then wham!

611
00:47:27,320 --> 00:47:28,860
That's it! Awesome, isn't it?

612
00:47:28,860 --> 00:47:30,483
Pardon?

613
00:47:30,483 --> 00:47:33,049
Yeah, wow! That's really awesome.

614
00:47:38,516 --> 00:47:40,384
[What does that
private investigator look like?]

615
00:47:46,560 --> 00:47:50,049
You dodge, you swing,
and then a backspin... wham!

616
00:47:57,108 --> 00:47:58,632
What's wrong?

617
00:47:58,632 --> 00:47:59,800
Are you okay?

618
00:47:59,800 --> 00:48:01,048
What? Oh...

619
00:48:01,048 --> 00:48:03,883
Oh, my phone slipped out of my pocket.

620
00:48:04,583 --> 00:48:06,508
Mr. Cha, is this okay?

621
00:48:06,508 --> 00:48:08,316
- The backspin.
- Yeah, that's fine.

622
00:48:08,316 --> 00:48:09,748
Looks great.

623
00:48:09,748 --> 00:48:10,748
- Think you can do it?
- Yes.

624
00:48:10,748 --> 00:48:11,816
You'll be okay, right?

625
00:48:11,816 --> 00:48:14,116
Yeah, no problem.

626
00:48:14,116 --> 00:48:15,940
Okay, perfect!

627
00:48:15,940 --> 00:48:17,949
Let's keep it exactly like this.

628
00:48:17,949 --> 00:48:20,916
- Got it.
- Hey, Sang Yong, move quickly!

629
00:49:04,583 --> 00:49:08,049
[Ye Ji]

630
00:49:11,883 --> 00:49:15,136
[Mom, did you confirm that
Ye Ji's mom deleted the video?]

631
00:49:29,812 --> 00:49:32,612
Are you okay?
Should I take you to the hospital?

632
00:49:32,612 --> 00:49:34,616
Never mind. I'm just tired.
Come on, let's get home. Hurry.

633
00:49:34,616 --> 00:49:36,316
Yes, yes.

634
00:50:06,248 --> 00:50:07,948
Huh?

635
00:50:08,792 --> 00:50:10,492
What?

636
00:51:03,116 --> 00:51:04,960
[Ultra-thin Non-Latex Condoms]

637
00:51:29,504 --> 00:51:31,416
Get home safely.

638
00:51:40,083 --> 00:51:42,749
What? Where is it?

639
00:51:46,792 --> 00:51:48,492
Oh my goodness.

640
00:51:57,020 --> 00:51:58,720
Dr. Joo!

641
00:52:01,116 --> 00:52:03,320
Why haven't you left yet?

642
00:52:03,320 --> 00:52:05,952
I was just trying to find my way out.

643
00:52:05,952 --> 00:52:08,883
I didn't drive here.

644
00:52:13,728 --> 00:52:15,428
Get in.

645
00:52:28,132 --> 00:52:29,912
Just for a moment, please.

646
00:52:29,912 --> 00:52:31,620
Oh, what is wrong with me?

647
00:52:31,620 --> 00:52:32,716
Just a little longer...

648
00:52:32,716 --> 00:52:34,912
I think I'll be ready soon.

649
00:52:34,912 --> 00:52:36,600
Jeez, what's happening to me?

650
00:52:36,600 --> 00:52:38,504
This has never happened before.

651
00:52:38,504 --> 00:52:39,576
- Dr. Joo.
- I'll be ready soon.

652
00:52:39,576 --> 00:52:41,116
- I'm not usually like this.
- Dr. Joo.

653
00:52:41,116 --> 00:52:42,256
I don't think this is right.

654
00:52:42,256 --> 00:52:43,816
No, no...

655
00:52:43,816 --> 00:52:46,108
- Kyung Hee, it'll work. Just a bit longer.
- Oh my...

656
00:52:46,108 --> 00:52:48,348
It'll be ready soon.

657
00:52:48,348 --> 00:52:50,048
Huh?

658
00:52:58,296 --> 00:52:59,996
Min Seo?

